    "created_at": "2019-09-11T20:01:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-11T20:01:06Z",
    "body": "I think showing the logical path is the sane default. \r\n\r\nGNU Coreutils `pwd` does this by just [trying to read the envar `PWD` and return that if it exists, falling back to hardlink resolution if it does not](https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/html_node/pwd-invocation.html#pwd-invocation). I don't think this would be too hard to emulate in starship.\r\n\r\n",
